            <ArticleTitle>Effects of calcitonin therapy on osteoporosis in patients with thalassemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this study was to evaluate the effects of calcitonin (CT) treatment on bone pain, osteoporosis, bone fractures and blood chemistry in thalassemic patients. Twenty-four patients with an age range of 10-24 years were included, 14 of whom received 100 IU CT and 250 mg calcium 3 times a week. The others (n = 10) were followed up as a control group with only routine thalassemia therapy. After 1 year of treatment, bone pain disappeared and radiological signs of osteoporosis had improved significantly (p &lt; 0.01) in the treatment group. CT has no important side effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
